  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"The return point and washing station are connected by a short route, and a transfer list can record crates.\", \"decision\": \"How should crates reach the washing station?\", \"goal\": \"Make cup lending and return convenient while keeping the available stock and volunteer work understandable.\", \"problem\": \"A neighborhood café wants to lend reusable cups at community gatherings and recover them afterward. It has a modest cup stock, washable collection crates, a simple lending record, and volunteers who can share short shifts. The plan concerns a small pilot with no deposit or sales system. Different decisions address separate moments in lending, return, and review.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nThe washing station requests the next crate through the transfer list when it has room. Transfers follow the washing station’s capacity.\nA volunteer moves crates at fixed intervals and updates the transfer list at both stations. A predictable round connects return and washing work.\nA volunteer takes a crate to the washing station whenever the return point marks it ready on the transfer list. Transfers follow the buildup of returned cups."
    }
  ],
